{
  "id": "multiway-17p-orientation",
  "measured": "2026-09-24",
  "published": false,
  "source": {
    "kind": "bench",
    "repro": "pnpm exec esbuild --bundle --platform=node --format=esm --target=node22 --outfile=/tmp/orient17p.mjs plugins/linear-comparative-view/benches/multiwayOrientation17p.probe.ts && node /tmp/orient17p.mjs, from the repo root (it rewrites this file) - the eight hosted hg38 liftOver PIFs of demos/hg38_vertebrates read through MultiPairwiseSyntenyAdapter over hg38 chr17:15,200,014-16,400,014 with the display's own fetch options (clip to the window, split at 10 kb indels), decided by `decideLaneFrames` with no incumbent at 1500 px.",
    "notes": "WHETHER EACH [rev] AT THE 17p FIGURE IS WHAT THE RAW ALIGNMENTS SAY. `drawn` is the lane's orientation on a fresh load, which is the figure's; `fallback` is the anchor-order sign sum the lane falls back on where the vote abstains; `votes against` is what the vote reads: the lane above while it shares at least three groups, else the anchor, which on a pairwise source is every lane but the top one, since each record names one mate. `shared` is how many groups the lane shares with that reference, and the two vote columns are the share of paired evidence reading backwards against it under the rule that ships (every pair, product of group weights) and under the rule it replaced on 2026-09-06 (neighbours, lighter run). The bp columns are the anchor bp of the lane's placements on the drawn contig by record strand, and `majority` names the heavier strand and its share: a share near 0.5 is a lane where the choice is arbitrary and hysteresis, not the data, holds it."
  },
